# esp32-aws-iot-fleet

Central jajera ESP32 firmware repo (PlatformIO + ESP-IDF). Not the talk deck
(`iot-everywhere-aws-talk`) and not the full lab (`aws-iot-walkthrough`).

## Do

- Prefer shared bootstrap here over copying firmware into demo/talk repos
- Add boards as new `[env:…]` + Thing Type + CI matrix entry
- Keep secrets out of git (`secrets.ini`, PEMs, keys)
- Build with `pio run -e <env>`; flash only when the operator asks

## Don't

- Commit `secrets.ini`, claim/device certs, or generated `sdkconfig.<env>`
- Redefine `build_flags` in `secrets.ini` (use `custom_aws_*` and `custom_wifi_*` only)
- Run mutating AWS CLI / IaC unless operator set `FLEET_ALLOW_AWS=1`
- Claim Arduino `rgbLedWrite` works on C61 (no RMT — SPI + DMA for WS2812)

## Defaults

- Default env: `esp32-c61`
- Profile/region examples: `sandbox` / `ap-southeast-2`
- Details: `.kiro/steering/` and `AGENTS.md`
